## Claude-specific

- Bypass mode still asks before an `rm` Claude Code cannot verify and before a command it cannot parse
  the way the shell will; a background subagent's prompt can wait for hours. So:
  - Give `rm` literal absolute paths and run it as its own command, not inside `sh -c` (including
    `podman run ... sh -c`). Never target run-time paths (`$D/*`, a `$(...)` result, a relative glob
    after a `cd`), `./*`, subdirectory globs, or home, `/tmp`, the working directory or its parents.
  - Write files with the Write tool, never a `cat`/`tee` heredoc in Bash (a hook denies it): literal
    heredoc text such as make's `$$(` trips the check. Run a program longer than a few lines from a
    scratchpad file. Avoid zsh-only syntax such as `${${x#a}%b}`.
- Don't probe credential or other-profile paths, even with `ls` or `test`: deny rules refuse the whole
  command.
